  "finding": "After giving the TP2 rank-local bulk prefill the same session-scoped GGUF linear dispatch context the resident bulk prefill establishes, all 15 layer-0 producer fields are bit-identical between the resident TP1 bulk teacher and the TP2 bulk candidate on identical input (sha256 306c076e9d0adb2214074d7e27d85d7249da2e38fc44614bd776c0cffbda9c5f), identical layer-0 weights, identical all-zero initial conv/recurrent state and the same chain_compact_peer_wave32 GDN mode. The previously measured divergence was the Q6_K attn_qkv projection (linear_qkv rel 3.73e-03, max_abs 0.25): the resident session runs it inside wmma_prefill_session(self.use_wmma_prefill=True) and the TP2 bulk path did not, so the same Q6_K weight at rows=64 resolved t16_wmma_prefill_bf16_bf16_out on the teacher and t16_gemv_decode_bf16_bf16_out on the candidate. The Q4_K attn_gate projection from the same launch group was already on its WMMA variant in both routes, which is why it stayed bit-identical. The candidate's resolve log now shows exactly one bulk context, equal to the teacher's; its remaining extra resolutions are the ambient-context decode warmup and the head projection.",
